{"status": "VERIFIED_ALL_DIMENSION_SIGNED_SUPPORT_LIFT_AND_UNSIGNED_MINOR_OBSTRUCTIONS", "analytic_statement": "For any positive generic d-coordinate base weights, adding m lowest coordinates with coefficients (sum(base)+1)*2^j preserves every old coupling sign under shift 2^(d+m-1)-2^(d-1). Hence a genuine K4 half-graph minor exists in every n>=6 and a genuine K33 half-graph subgraph exists in every n>=8.", "scope": "Excludes universal series-parallel/treewidth-two and planar half-graph shortcuts. No odd-K5 signed minor, failure of weak bipartiteness, or failure of a positive-density RLC lower bound is inferred.", "violations": 0, "seconds": 1.3347272190003423, "audit_sha256": "a7b3f4aedf6f6d1a4adc6555ac096453a5e20952462599c97457c35ea3f6cdfe"}
